<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 166 0 R
/T (Counter bugs. If the counter is incremented before the blank check, blank entries are counted as attempts and a customer is locked out unfairly. If the increment is placed after a continue, or is forgotten, the loop condition never becomes false and a kiosk that keeps receiving blank entries loops forever. The counter must be updated exactly once, after a real entry is received and before the result is checked. )
/E (Counter bugs. If the counter is incremented before the blank check, blank entries are counted as attempts and a customer is locked out unfairly. If the increment is placed after a continue, or is forgotten, the loop condition never becomes false and a kiosk that keeps receiving blank entries loops forever. The counter must be updated exactly once, after a real entry is received and before the result is checked. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
399 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 166 0 R
/T (Changed condition. Two extra attempts are allowed after a correct security answer. The while loop keeps a variable limit \(3, becoming 5\) and a flag so that the security question is asked only once; when attempts reach the limit the loop asks the security question and either raises the limit or locks the account. )
/E (Changed condition. Two extra attempts are allowed after a correct security answer. The while loop keeps a variable limit \(3, becoming 5\) and a flag so that the security question is asked only once; when attempts reach the limit the loop asks the security question and either raises the limit or locks the account. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
