<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 166 0 R
/T (Alternative concept \(recursion\). A function can call itself for the next attempt with attempt + 1, the base cases being a correct OTP or attempt > 3. Time is O\(a\) for a attempts in every version; recursion uses O\(a\) stack space because each pending call stays on the call stack, while the while and for loops use O\(1\) space. )
/E (Alternative concept \(recursion\). A function can call itself for the next attempt with attempt + 1, the base cases being a correct OTP or attempt > 3. Time is O\(a\) for a attempts in every version; recursion uses O\(a\) stack space because each pending call stays on the call stack, while the while and for loops use O\(1\) space. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [9]
>>
