830 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 181 0 R
/T (Scope. A local name exists only inside the function that assigns it. A global name belongs to the module. A nonlocal name belongs to an enclosing function and lets an inner function rebind it. Assigning to a global inside a function makes Python treat the name as local, so counter += 1 raises UnboundLocalError unless global counter is declared. Global variables are usually avoided because any function can change them, which hides dependencies and makes code hard to test. )
/E (Scope. A local name exists only inside the function that assigns it. A global name belongs to the module. A nonlocal name belongs to an enclosing function and lets an inner function rebind it. Assigning to a global inside a function makes Python treat the name as local, so counter += 1 raises UnboundLocalError unless global counter is declared. Global variables are usually avoided because any function can change them, which hides dependencies and makes code hard to test. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
