/Title (Slicing. s[-4:] returns the last four characters, which is the 4-digit number for both lengths. s[4:-4] returns what lies between the first four and the last four characters: for a 9-character number it returns 1 letter \(for example 'A'\), and for a 10-character number it returns 2 letters \(for example 'AB'\). Alternative concept \(regular expression\). re.fullmatch\(r"[A-Z]{2}[0-9]{2}[A-Z]{1,2}[0-9]{4}", reg\) does the whole validation in one line. Both approaches scan the L characters once, so the time is O\(L\) and the space O\(1\) for both. The regular expression is shorter and easier to change \(a different series length changes only {1,2}\), but harder to read for beginners; the slicing version is longer and a change needs both the length check and the slice positions, but every rule is explicit and needs no import.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2081 0 R
/Prev 2089 0 R
>>
endobj
