/Title (Correct design. Use None as the default and create a new list inside the function body \(if order is None: order = []\). None is immutable, so nothing is shared between calls.)
/Dest [31 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2207 0 R
/Prev 2211 0 R
/Next 2219 0 R
>>
endobj
2216 0 obj
<<
/Title (Scope. A local name exists only inside the function that assigns it. A global name belongs to the module. A nonlocal name belongs to an enclosing function and lets an inner function rebind it. Assigning to a global inside a function makes Python treat the name as local, so counter += 1 raises UnboundLocalError unless global counter is declared. Global variables are usually avoided because any function can change them, which hides dependencies and makes code hard to test.)
/Dest [31 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2207 0 R
/Prev 2220 0 R
/Next 2212 0 R
>>
endobj
